{"title":"User：Icosahedron0288","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Introduction\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Introduction</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Remark\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Remark</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#About_Me\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">About Me</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Goals\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Goals</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Achievements\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Achievements</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Failures\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Failures</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Problem_of_the_Week\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem of the Week</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Aops_Contributions\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Aops Contributions</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Created_Pages\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Created Pages</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Solution_Contributions\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution Contributions</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Introduction\">Introduction</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=User%EF%BC%9AIcosahedron0288&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Introduction\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Hi, I'm <b>Icosahedron0288</b>, a friend of xue1. Welcome to my page. Below is some information about me and a list of all my AoPS contributions, including a weekly problem I made myself. Before you continue, here is a truncated conical frustum of orange juice topped with a spherical cap of foam: 🥤🍊🥤\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Remark\">Remark</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=User%EF%BC%9AIcosahedron0288&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Remark\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>In case you're wondering, my user tag \"Icosahedron0288\" is inspired by the 3D geometric shape, the icosahedron—a regular polyhedron with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> triangular faces, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/1/651ba418a810d971dbc8a326d49a71fe1541fae0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> edges, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> vertices. The \"0288\" refers to the integer 28 (with a leading zero), which is a perfect number since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/c/f0c14e89c272bea52723b1871473e9eff9f99b3a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$28 = 1+2+4+7+14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"188\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>Also, in case you want your drink(🍊🥤🍊) to be icier, here are 28 blocks of <b>perfect</b> ice:🧊🧊🧊🧊🧊🧊🧊🧊🧊🧊🧊🧊🧊🧊🧊🧊🧊🧊🧊🧊🧊🧊🧊🧊🧊🧊🧊🧊\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"About_Me\">About Me</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=User%EF%BC%9AIcosahedron0288&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: About Me\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><b> Basics:</b> Age 13, Born California(Irvine), Male, Y9</li>\n<li><b> Top 3 Best Friends:</b> Jaesung, Lucas, Ethan(xue1)</li>\n<li><b>Current Focus:</b> AMC10</li>\n<li><b>Status:</b> Running out of time to finish remaining AMC10 past papers</li>\n<li><b>Favorite Topics:</b> Counting &amp; Probability <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/f/c0f2b8e02812dd6278501da3698b07563864df3d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cap$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"11\" height=\"11\" /> Algebra (maybe?).</li>\n<li><b> Least Favorite Topics: </b> Number Theory  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/f/c0f2b8e02812dd6278501da3698b07563864df3d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cap$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"11\" height=\"11\" /> Floor Functions  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/f/c0f2b8e02812dd6278501da3698b07563864df3d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cap$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"11\" height=\"11\" /> Fractional Parts</li>\n<li><b>Hobbies:</b> Math, chess, and writing math problems about<b>xuxu</b>.</li>\n<li><b>Favorite Mathematician:</b> Terrence Tao</li>\n<li><b> Favorite Problem:</b>  <i>2020 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 13A</i>: frog sitting at the point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/2/69273482bff8727194f6407e55ac1bfa94d9c555.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1, 2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" /> begins a sequence of jumps, where each jump is parallel to one of the coordinate axes and has length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and the direction of each jump (up, down, right, or left) is chosen independently at random. The sequence ends when the frog reaches a side of the square with vertices <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/c/b8cafb7774031874f23ebb8f88f9d4bac2439d1b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0,0), (0,4), (4,4),$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"141\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/6/b86f58cb609fa753024f1173510c877971f8e4e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(4,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />. What is the probability that the sequence of jumps ends on a vertical side of the square?</li></ul>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/3/8a3e088ff5b553720349acc5f41c3270d925fa32.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\frac12\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ \\frac 58\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ \\frac 23\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ \\frac34\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ \\frac 78$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"367\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Goals\">Goals</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=User%EF%BC%9AIcosahedron0288&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Goals\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li>110+ For UKMT SMC</li>\n<li>90-120 for AMC10</li>\n<li>Get higher chess elo (even though I dont play often)</li>\n<li>Learn how to use LaTeX fluidly</li>\n<li>Current books: <i>Intermmediate Algebra, AMC10 Preperation Book, Klara and the Sun, Wordly Wise 3000 Book 9</i></li></ul>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Achievements\">Achievements</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=User%EF%BC%9AIcosahedron0288&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Achievements\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li>Gold Medal for 2026 UKMT Junior Math Challenge, score:112/135</li>\n<li>Silver Medal &amp; Best in Year for 2026 UKMT Junior Mathematical Olympiad, score:42/50</li>\n<li>Perfect Score on the ISEE Middle Level Math section</li>\n<li>Getting 8/8s for my Y7-8 school math tests</li></ul>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Failures\">Failures</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=User%EF%BC%9AIcosahedron0288&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Failures\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li>9/10 for 2025 AMC8</li>\n<li>14/25 for 2026 AMC8</li>\n<li>29 /60 for CEIMC</li>\n<li>Getting the easy last question wrong on the first Y9 school math test</li></ul>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_of_the_Week\">Problem of the Week</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=User%EF%BC%9AIcosahedron0288&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Problem of the Week\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>An advanced civilization from the Andromeda Galaxy has detected Earth just a few months ago, and now they are going to conduct experiments to see how good humans are at math. To do this, they randomly extracted a young mathematician from a group of 2000 elites, which turns out to be Xuxu. Xuxu is being escorted to a platform where he discovered a line of 2026 individuals. Among the 2026, there are males, females, and 2 hyper-advanced extraterrestrial humanoids, lined up in the following manner: no more than two males can appear consecutively, no more than five females can appear consecutively, and the humanoids will be at both ends, to catch anyone escaping. The gender of the person standing at the two ends of the line (between the humanoids) must be male. Now, Xuxu's only job is to calculate how many ways this is possible, before he gets sent to the next challenge. What interval does his answer lie in?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/b/e5b126a7ba37aa08632b0232df78042b16e1b46a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ [10^{100}, 10^{200}]\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ [10^{200}, 10^{300}]\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ [10^{300}, 10^{400}]\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ [10^{400}, 10^{500}]\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ [10^{500}, 10^{600}]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"785\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>Difficulty: 5/10\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Aops_Contributions\">Aops Contributions</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=User%EF%BC%9AIcosahedron0288&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Aops Contributions\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Created_Pages\">Created Pages</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=User%EF%BC%9AIcosahedron0288&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Created Pages\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<table class=\"wikitable sortable\" style=\"width:100%; text-align:left;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<th style=\"background:#f2f2f2; width:45%;\">Page Link\n</th>\n<th style=\"background:#f2f2f2; width:20%;\">Type / Category\n</th>\n<th style=\"background:#f2f2f2; width:35%;\">Creation Context\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_(Regional)_Problems\" title=\"2026 AMC 8 (Regional) Problems\">2026 AMC 8 (Regional) Problems</a></td>\n<td>Main Directory</td>\n<td>Created 11 Aug 2026\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_BmMT_Individual_Problems\" title=\"2026 BmMT Individual Problems\">2026 BmMT Individual Problems</a></td>\n<td>Contest Hub Page</td>\n<td>Created 23 Sep 2026\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_BmMT_Individual_Problems\" title=\"2021 BmMT Individual Problems\">2021 BmMT Individual Problems</a></td>\n<td>Contest Hub Page</td>\n<td>Created 24 Sep 2026\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_BmMT_Individual_Problems\" title=\"2022 BmMT Individual Problems\">2022 BmMT Individual Problems</a></td>\n<td>Contest Hub Page</td>\n<td>Created 24 Sep 2026\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_BmMT_Individual_Problems\" title=\"2023 BmMT Individual Problems\">2023 BmMT Individual Problems</a></td>\n<td>Contest Hub Page</td>\n<td>Created 23 Sep 2026\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_BmMT_Individual_Problems\" title=\"2024 BmMT Individual Problems\">2024 BmMT Individual Problems</a></td>\n<td>Contest Hub Page</td>\n<td>Created 23 Sep 2026\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_BmMT_Individual_Problems\" title=\"2025 BmMT Individual Problems\">2025 BmMT Individual Problems</a></td>\n<td>Contest Hub Page</td>\n<td>Created 23 Sep 2026\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Berkeley_Mini_Math_Tornament_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"Berkeley Mini Math Tornament Problems and Solutions\">Berkeley Mini Math Tornament Problems and Solutions</a></td>\n<td>Main Directory</td>\n<td>Created 23 Sep 2026\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Berkeley_Math_Tournament_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"Berkeley Math Tournament Problems and Solutions\">Berkeley Math Tournament Problems and Solutions</a></td>\n<td>Main Directory</td>\n<td>Created 23 Sep 2026\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Magic_Square_Association\" title=\"Magic Square Association\">Magic Square Association</a></td>\n<td>Directory / Article</td>\n<td>Created 11 Aug 2026\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_Contributions\">Solution Contributions</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=User%EF%BC%9AIcosahedron0288&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Solution Contributions\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<table class=\"wikitable sortable\" style=\"width:100%; text-align:left;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<th style=\"background:#f2f2f2; width:45%;\">Problem Page Link\n</th>\n<th style=\"background:#f2f2f2; width:20%;\">Solution\n</th>\n<th style=\"background:#f2f2f2; width:35%;\">Description\n</th></tr>\n\n<tr>\n<th colspan=\"3\" style=\"background:#e6f2ff; text-align:left;\">AMC 10 / AMC 12\n</th></tr>\n\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2014 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 6\">2014 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 6</a></td>\n<td>Solution 8</td>\n<td>Formula Version\n</td></tr>\n\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2014 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 10\">2014 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 10</a></td>\n<td>Solution 2</td>\n<td>Similar to 1, Less Math Jargon\n</td></tr>\n\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2014 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 20\">2014 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 20</a></td>\n<td>Solution 5</td>\n<td>Completing the Square\n</td></tr>\n\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 22\">2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 22</a></td>\n<td>Solution 4</td>\n<td>Explaining the Martingale Shortcut\n</td></tr>\n\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2015 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 19\">2015 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 19</a></td>\n<td>Solution 6<